feat(#93): add xeniapolis.de source map inventory for migration completeness

Adds scripts/xeniapolis-source-map.ts, a re-runnable BFS crawler (following
the validate-okf.ts script/test convention) that walks xeniapolis.de from its
root, transitively discovering every frame/menu/start/tour page without
needing to special-case those patterns as seeds. Generates
docs/reference/xeniapolis-source-map.{json,md} — 342 records, one per
reachable source URL — so #92's migration completeness can be checked
against this inventory instead of asserted.

Each record carries url, httpStatus, title (decoded from the site's actual
ISO-8859-1 bytes, despite the mismatched utf-8 Content-Type header it serves),
targetPath, assets[], underConstruction, and notes. Target paths follow the
existing (if inconsistent) src/content/docs/xeniapolis/<slug>/ folder
convention; two already-migrated pages were hand-verified by content
comparison (mar/marstart.html, zen/zenstart.html) and two more turned out to
be many-to-one aggregates of a numbered page sequence into a single MDX file
(ann/kurzueb1-5.html -> kurzuebersicht.mdx; kon/ewelt2*.html ->
konstellationen-beim-uebergang-zur-nformationsgesellschaft.mdx, confirmed by
matching each source page's <title> against a `##` heading in the MDX).
Pages outside the Stadtviertel/Zentrum structure (telepol/, ~mib/, broken
nested links) are flagged "needs manual triage" rather than assigned a
plausible-but-wrong path.

Reviewed against origin/epic/92-migrate-xeniapolis-de via /code-review;
fixed two spec-axis gaps it found (a dead extensionless link with no
recognized extension was being silently dropped instead of recorded; now
anything not a known asset extension is treated as a page so no reachable
URL vanishes from the inventory) and two standards-axis nits (test
assertions and process.stdout/argv access now match validate-okf's exact
style; a duplicated path-segment split was factored into one helper).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
EOF
)"
